text:
sam: heads-up — found a mismatch in the /v1/generate API examples. The example request shows "attachments" as a single object and "metadata" as a map that is always present. Runtime + SDKs expect attachments: [] (array) and metadata: null | object. This trips the Go SDK validation and some older Ruby clients.

kevin: can you paste the offending snippet?

sam: sure — bad example from docs page:```
{
  "model": "redwood/gpt-1",
  "prompt": "summarize...",
  "attachments": {
    "filename": "notes.txt",
    "size": 1024
  },
  "metadata": {
    "user": "alice"
  }
}
```

sam: runtime wants:```
{
  "model": "redwood/gpt-1",
  "prompt": "summarize...",
  "attachments": [
    {
      "filename": "notes.txt",
      "size": 1024
    }
  ],
  "metadata": null
}
```

maria: ack. that explains the 400s I saw in the support queue earlier today. we should: 1) update the openapi example, 2) sync python/go/ruby snippets, 3) add a short migration note saying old clients that sent single-object attachments must wrap it in an array or send "attachments: []".

kevin: I'll take the openapi + SDK snippet changes. do we need a docs test to catch this going forward? maybe run examples through the request validator in CI.

sam: yes please — there's already a unit in docs/tests/validate_examples.py that fails for this; i can add a test case showing object->array mismatch and link it. i'll open the PR for the examples update and migration note: https://github.com/redwood/docs/pull/4827

olivia: docs-bot: preview build for PR 4827 is up: https://deploy-preview.redwood.dev/4827 :white_check_mark:

kevin: on it. i'll update the Go snippet to show the array and include a short note in the code comment. ETA EOD. @maria can you draft the short customer-facing migration blurb?

maria: yep will draft and post in #customer-success for review.

sam: thanks team — assigning follow-ups: kevin (openapi + SDK snippets), sam (test + PR), maria (migration blurb). ping here when done. :thumbsup:
